  "acceptance": "Extend the round-3 file release/Poincare/L4/GeodesicComparison/SturmZeroCount.lean (which already proves the one-sided strict-excess zero existence, the anchored dichotomy, the constructed shifted model sturmModel with its Jacobi-solution structure, and the witnesses) to genuine TWO-SIDED zero interlacing for the scalar Jacobi equation. Required content: (1) upper-curvature spacing bound: if a < b are consecutive zeros of u (u a = u b = 0, u > 0 on (a,b)) and k <= K2 on [a,b] with k < K2 somewhere, prove sqrt(K2) * (b - a) > pi, i.e. the model zero a + pi/sqrt(K2) lies strictly before b (consume D12 sturm_zero_comparison with the model as u1 and u as u2, using the constructed sturmModel from SturmZeroCount.lean); (2) the equality case: if k = K2 identically on [a,b] then b - a = pi/sqrt(K2) -- at least for the constant-curvature model, proved from the model's own zero structure; (3) combine with the round-3 lower bound to state the two-sided interval: pi/sqrt(K2) <= b - a (with the strict-excess refinement) under k <= K2, cross-checked numerically against sin(sqrt(2) t) on (0, pi/sqrt(2)) with K2 = 2; (4) witnesses showing both the strict and equality cases, and that the hypotheses are satisfiable. Acceptance evidence: compiling module(s), source hashes, compile exits, fail-closed axiom audit with cones subset {propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound}, explicit non-vacuous witnesses, and an adversarial semantic review confirming the statements are not restatements of the engine and that no manifold-level claim is made. Do not assume the target spacing bound as a hypothesis and do not duplicate SturmZeroCount.lean content.",
